  "_comment": "Alias resolution is exact-string, applied to an already normalized value (trimmed, lowercased, whitespace collapsed, surrounding punctuation stripped). Keys are normalized aliases, values are the canonical form that both the model output and the gold value are resolved to before comparison. It is never substring replacement and aliases never chain. There is deliberately no alias for the bare first name Ravi: two people on two different teams carry it, so only the full names and the surnames resolve. The two names of the renamed product resolve to two different canonical values, because a question about January and a question about now have different answers. Every real issue in the WRN project also aliases its title to its id, because a question that asks which issue tracks something expects the id and Slack only ever names the issue by its title; the 14 near-duplicate decoy issues are deliberately left out, so answering with a decoy title stays wrong.",
